// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/legacy_retirement.t27 -- what "retired" means in this repository
; This contract owns one distinction and nothing else: DATA that was hidden is not the same
; thing as a SURFACE that is still reachable. It is the contract for DECISIONS.md D5 and D19
; and for the open issue #2 under epic #26. It states the three partial retirement states this
; tree actually exhibits, the one completed state that makes them legible, the rule that a
; hidden row never retires a live surface, and the allowlist mechanism D19 and epic #26 both
; require -- heritage is hidden rather than deleted, and anything kept is named with a reason.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). The two retirement migrations disagree about what retirement is,
; and no contract said so. That absence was RE-MEASURED on 2026-09-21 against the finished
; 43-file corpus and it still holds, but only in its narrow form, so the narrow form is what is
; written: 16 of the other 42 files now contain the word "retire", and NONE of them declares the
; distinction this file owns. The grep that decides it is not the word but the state machine --
; retirement_state, STATE_DATA_HIDDEN and STATE_SURFACE_LIVE appear in no other file. The 16 are
; something else: the edge REUSES_LEGACY_RETIREMENT_ID pointing here, the bike-unit STATUS
; "retired" that turbobaby/availability owns, and the retired "skate" spelling that
; turbobaby/ride-game and turbobaby/star-award own. A reader who greps the WORD gets 16 and must
; not read that as sixteen contracts ruling on retirement; the word is shared, the subject is not.
; migrations/083_drop_cannabis_catalog.sql drops six tables outright
; (:82-84 and :88-90). migrations/085_unpublish_woody_catalog.sql deletes no row and drops no
; table: it issues six visibility UPDATEs (:25-30) and one in-place rename (:36-38), and says
; at :12 and :19-21 that the rows are kept and the flags are reversible. Underneath both, the
; surface never moved. src/api/mod.rs:89 still merges the legacy catalog router, whose routes()
; at src/api/catalog.rs:13-59 declares 27 HTTP routes over accessories, accessory sets, tea
; products, tea sets and strain sets -- routes whose tables now answer with rows that were
; flipped invisible, not removed. src/ui/routes.rs still declares eight legacy paths that
; resolve to legacy screens. So the live count that forces this file is a ZERO: of the eight
; legacy screen routes and the 44 legacy HTTP routes measured below, migrations 083 and 085
; retired NONE. They were data decisions, and a data decision cannot retire a surface.
; --
; The sharpest single measurement is the allowlist. tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:49-82 holds
; four entries excusing shipped code that still reads a table 083 dropped. All four name the
; SAME table, strains -- so one of the six dropped tables carries every surviving reader and
; the other five carry none. That is the third state: the table is gone, the reader is not,
; and what keeps the tree honest is not the drop but the named excuse.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED (four survey citations opened and checked on 2026-09-21).
;   1. "about 23 routes" in src/api/catalog.rs:16-58 is 27. A count of route declarations in
;      that file returns 27, and every one of them is inside routes(); the declarations span
;      :16-58 and the function spans :13-59. The count is pinned below as 27.
;   2. "/game renders a cannabis-era shop title to any customer who opens it (src/ui/game/
;      shop_game.rs:1)" does not survive its own citation. Line 1 of that file is a SOURCE
;      COMMENT, which no customer can see. The component's rsx root at src/ui/game/
;      shop_game.rs:679 opens with a coin HUD and declares no title node at all, and the one
;      title key the repository defines for this screen family, T_GAME_TITLE at src/trios/
;      i18n.rs:345, resolves to a TurboBaby string in both locales (:1007 and :1606) and is
;      referenced by no screen -- a search for T_GAME_TITLE under src/ returns only i18n.rs
;      itself. A search of src/ui/game/shop_game.rs for a quoted string carrying the old shop's
;      name returns zero. What IS true, and is what this contract counts, is coarser and worse:
;      the ROUTE is live. src/ui/routes.rs:64 declares /game, :285 mounts GameScreen, src/ui/
;      screens/game_screen.rs:15 mounts the legacy component, and 1957 lines of a shop-and-
;      planters game render to any customer who opens the path. The surface is the defect; the
;      title was not.
;   3. "tests/retired_table_wiring.rs, survey :49-81" is :49-82 -- the const opens at 49 and
;      closes at 82. The size, 4, is what this file pins, not the span.
;   4. "about 9523 LOC across 26 of the 181 src/*.rs files". 181 is right: every .rs file under
;      src/ counts to 181. 9523 across 26 does not reproduce -- no TRACKED file in the tree
;      carries the number 9523, and no nameable file list sums to it. This file therefore pins
;      its OWN reproducible measurement instead: 25 named legacy-domain source files totalling
;      9193 lines, the set being the eight screens behind the live legacy routes, the four UI
;      game modules and the set card, the three API modules that serve them, five entities, and
;      the four trios and db modules of the strain, quest, tea and pack domains. A number whose
;      file list cannot be named is not evidence, so 9523 is reported unconfirmed, not copied.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It implements no route, describes no screen, carries no Cyrillic
; copy and names no deletion date -- issue #2 is open and the order of retirement is the
; owner's call, refused explicitly below. It restates nothing a sibling owns: the delivery-zone
; rename that rides along in the same migration 085 belongs to turbobaby/delivery-terms, which
; owns ZONE_RENAME_MIGRATION and ZONE_ROWS_KEPT_REASON, and is neither re-decided nor counted
; here; the mount status of the orphaned catch asset belongs to turbobaby/game-score, which owns
; CATCH_ERA_ASSET_IS_MOUNTED; the retirement of the skate spelling belongs to turbobaby/ride-game
; and turbobaby/star-award, the latter owning RETAINED_LEGACY_SOURCE, so no /skate path enters
; any count below; and the word "retired"
; as a BIKE UNIT STATUS is turbobaby/availability's, which owns STATUS_RETIRED and STATUS_NAMES, a
; different subject that this file never touches. Each sibling is named by ID and declaration
; rather than by line: all three of these were line citations, all three still pointed at the
; right subject on 2026-09-21, and all three would have rotted on the next edit next door. It carries no renter, handle, phone, key
; code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note (D14): every constant here is a table
; name, a path, a route pattern or a count.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-legacy-retirement;

pub const KIND : str = "retirement-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/legacy-retirement";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby legacy retirement states";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const DECISIONS : str = "DECISIONS.md D5, D19";
pub const ISSUE : str = "#2";
pub const EPIC : str = "#26";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";

; --- Where every number below was read ----------------------------------------------------------
pub const DROP_MIGRATION : str = "migrations/083_drop_cannabis_catalog.sql";
pub const HIDE_MIGRATION : str = "migrations/085_unpublish_woody_catalog.sql";
pub const PUBLIC_ROUTER : str = "src/api/mod.rs";
pub const LEGACY_HTTP_MODULE : str = "src/api/catalog.rs";
pub const CLIENT_ROUTER : str = "src/ui/routes.rs";
pub const ALLOWLIST_WITNESS : str = "tests/retired_table_wiring.rs";

; --- Reuse: what this file consumes instead of restating ----------------------------------------
; Each ID is the owner of a decision this contract needs as an abstract parameter. Naming the
; owner is the whole of the dependency; no table, threshold or route of theirs is copied here.
pub const REUSES_BOT_SURFACE_ID : str = "turbobaby/bot-surface";
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID : str = "turbobaby/catalog-api";
pub const REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/availability";
pub const REUSES_PUBLICATION_ID : str = "turbobaby/publication";
pub const REUSES_DELIVERY_TERMS_ID : str = "turbobaby/delivery-terms";
pub const REUSES_GAME_SCORE_ID : str = "turbobaby/game-score";
pub const REUSES_RIDE_GAME_ID : str = "turbobaby/ride-game";
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT : u8 = 7;

; --- The states ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Five values, of which three are the partial states this tree actually exhibits. STATE_LIVE is
; the absence of any retirement and STATE_FULLY_RETIRED is the one completed case, present
; exactly once: the garden route. It is declared because the three partial states are only
; legible against a finished one -- without it "retired" would have no value to mean finished.
pub const STATE_LIVE : u8 = 0;
pub const STATE_DATA_HIDDEN : u8 = 1;
pub const STATE_SURFACE_LIVE : u8 = 2;
pub const STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED : u8 = 3;
pub const STATE_FULLY_RETIRED : u8 = 4;
pub const STATE_COUNT : u8 = 5;

pub const PARTIAL_STATE_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES : [3]str = ["data_hidden", "surface_live", "reader_allowlisted"];

; Precedence is the contract. A reachable legacy surface outranks every data decision taken
; underneath it, because a customer reaches the surface and never reaches the decision.
pub fn retirement_state(legacy_surface_reachable: bool, table_dropped: bool, reader_kept: bool, rows_hidden: bool) u8 {
    if (legacy_surface_reachable) {
        return STATE_SURFACE_LIVE;
    }
    if (table_dropped and reader_kept) {
        return STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED;
    }
    if (table_dropped) {
        return STATE_FULLY_RETIRED;
    }
    if (rows_hidden) {
        return STATE_DATA_HIDDEN;
    }
    return STATE_LIVE;
}

pub fn state_is_known(state: u8) bool {
    return state < STATE_COUNT;
}

; The rule, stated as a function so it can be checked rather than believed: only the completed
; state is a retired surface. Hiding rows is not it, and an allowlisted reader is not it either.
pub fn surface_is_retired(legacy_surface_reachable: bool, table_dropped: bool, reader_kept: bool, rows_hidden: bool) bool {
    return retirement_state(legacy_surface_reachable, table_dropped, reader_kept, rows_hidden) == STATE_FULLY_RETIRED;
}

; What a data migration is entitled to change, and what it is not. The answer is a constant
; false: 083 and 085 chose opposite sides of the data question on consecutive numbers, and
; neither choice moved a route by one line.
pub fn data_decision_changes_the_surface(rows_hidden: bool, table_dropped: bool) bool {
    return false;
}

; --- Migration 085: heritage is hidden, not deleted ----------------------------------------------
; The shape D19 mandates. Rows survive, tables survive, and at least one visibility flag moves.
; HIDDEN_TABLES is the migration's own order: one is_public UPDATE at :25 and five is_available
; UPDATEs at :26-30. The delivery_zones rename at :36-38 is deliberately absent from this list;
; it is a rename rather than a hiding, and its owner is turbobaby/delivery-terms.
pub const HIDDEN_TABLE_COUNT : u8 = 6;
pub const HIDDEN_TABLES : [6]str = ["events", "accessories", "accessory_sets", "tea_products", "tea_sets", "sets"];
pub const HIDING_VISIBILITY_UPDATES : u16 = 6;
pub const HIDING_ROW_DELETES : u16 = 0;
pub const HIDING_TABLE_DROPS : u16 = 0;

pub fn hiding_migration_is_conformant(row_deletes: u16, table_drops: u16, visibility_updates: u16) bool {
    if (row_deletes > 0 or table_drops > 0) {
        return false;
    }
    return visibility_updates > 0;
}

; Reversibility is the property D19 bought with the flags, and it is the reason a hidden row is
; not a retirement: what a flag did, a flag undoes, with no migration and no deploy.
pub fn hidden_data_is_reversible(rows_kept: bool, flag_is_the_only_change: bool) bool {
    return rows_kept and flag_is_the_only_change;
}

; --- Migration 083: six tables dropped -----------------------------------------------------------
; Declaration order is the migration's own: children first at :82-84, then the garden trio at
; :88-90. The split below is the measurement that matters -- one dropped table carries every
; surviving reader and five carry none.
; THIS FILE OWNS THIS NUMBER. turbobaby/bot-surface needs it for its carousel tripwire and keeps
; it as a MARKED COPY (its LEGACY_TABLES_DROPPED_BY_THAT_MIGRATION), pinned to this value by a
; drift invariant on that side. The retirement owner is here, so a change to migration 083 is
; edited here FIRST and the copy follows; the invariant next door fails the gate if it does not.
pub const DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT : u8 = 6;
pub const DROPPED_TABLES : [6]str = ["lab_certificates", "strain_reviews", "strains", "garden_rewards", "garden_plants", "garden_config"];
pub const DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_A_SURVIVING_READER : u8 = 1;
pub const DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_NO_READER : u8 = 5;
pub const DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = true;
pub const DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPIED_BY_ID : str = "turbobaby/bot-surface";
pub const DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPY_DECLARATION : str = "LEGACY_TABLES_DROPPED_BY_THAT_MIGRATION";

; --- The allowlist, as the mechanism D19 and epic #26 require ------------------------------------
; Four entries at tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:49-82, each a path, a table and a prose reason.
; Its SIZE and its RULE are pinned; its contents are not, because the contents are a to-do list
; that shrinks and the rule is the contract -- a small reviewed list, no global replacement.
; Three of that file's nine tests guard the list (:450, :476, :495); the other six pin what its
; detector sees -- 3 module-reference shapes (:569), 5 table-position keywords (:303).
; THIS FILE OWNS THIS NUMBER TOO, on the same terms: turbobaby/bot-surface carries it as the
; marked copy LEGACY_SURVIVOR_ENTRY_COUNT under its own drift invariant. The allowlist is a
; to-do list that shrinks, so this is the number most likely to move, and it moves here first.
pub const ALLOWLIST_SIZE : u8 = 4;
pub const ALLOWLIST_SIZE_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = true;
pub const ALLOWLIST_SIZE_COPY_DECLARATION : str = "LEGACY_SURVIVOR_ENTRY_COUNT";
pub const ALLOWLIST_DISTINCT_TABLES : u8 = 1;
pub const ALLOWLIST_REASON_MIN_CHARS : u16 = 40;
pub const ALLOWLIST_CHECK_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const ALLOWLIST_DETECTION_SHAPE_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const ALLOWLIST_TABLE_POSITION_KEYWORDS : u8 = 5;

; --- The absence this file still closes, re-measured ---------------------------------------------
; "No contract said so" is the load-bearing absence of this file, and a false absence is the one
; thing a reader trusts without checking, so it carries a date and a denominator rather than a
; bare word. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 over the finished corpus, this file excluded: the WORD
; reaches 16 files, the SUBJECT reaches none. The second number is the claim; the first is here
; so that a reader who greps the word and gets 16 can see that the two were counted separately.
pub const CORPUS_FILE_COUNT : u8 = 43;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE : u8 = 42;
pub const SPECS_CONTAINING_THE_WORD_RETIRE_2026_09_21 : u8 = 16;
pub const SPECS_DECLARING_THE_RETIREMENT_DISTINCTION_2026_09_21 : u8 = 0;
pub const THE_WORD_IS_SHARED_THE_SUBJECT_IS_NOT : bool = true;

; The reason floor is read from the witness itself: every_survivor_carries_a_reason asserts a
; reason longer than 40 characters at tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:499, so exactly 40 fails.
pub fn allowlist_entry_is_valid(names_path: bool, names_table: bool, reason_chars: u16, still_matches: bool) bool {
    if (reason_chars <= ALLOWLIST_REASON_MIN_CHARS) {
        return false;
    }
    return names_path and names_table and still_matches;
}

; Checked from both ends, which is what stops the list becoming a hiding place: an unlisted
; reference fails (:450), and a listed entry matching nothing fails (:476). A list that can go
; stale is a to-do list; one that cannot is a place things go to hide.
pub fn allowlist_is_sound(every_reference_listed: bool, every_entry_still_matches: bool, every_entry_has_reason: bool) bool {
    return every_reference_listed and every_entry_still_matches and every_entry_has_reason;
}

; D19's second half: anything kept must be NAMED with a reason. Keeping without naming is not a
; smaller version of keeping with a reason; it is the thing the allowlist exists to forbid.
pub fn keeping_is_permitted(named_in_allowlist: bool, reason_chars: u16) bool {
    return named_in_allowlist and reason_chars > ALLOWLIST_REASON_MIN_CHARS;
}

; The retired set is DERIVED from the migrations in filename order rather than listed, so a
; table a future migration drops inherits the guard with nobody remembering it, and a table
; dropped then recreated is live again. The premise assert at :385 is the third leg: if the
; migrations stop retiring the anchor table, the guard says its premise changed rather than
; passing on an empty set.
pub fn retired_set_is_trustworthy(derived_from_migrations: bool, honours_recreation: bool, premise_asserted: bool) bool {
    return derived_from_migrations and honours_recreation and premise_asserted;
}

; --- The surface that never moved ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Eight client paths still resolve to legacy screens (src/ui/routes.rs:35, :37, :62, :64, :74,
; :76, :78, :80, handlers at :158, :167, :257, :285, :303, :312, :321, :330). Two further legacy
; paths, /sets at :31 and /sommelier at :33, are REPOINTED to the live catalog at :136-154 and
; are counted apart: a kept path with a deleted screen is a different animal from a kept screen,
; and what a live catalog is belongs to turbobaby/catalog-api and turbobaby/availability.
pub const LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 8;
pub const LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES : [8]str = ["/accessories", "/tea", "/quest/:id", "/game", "/treasure-hunt", "/ar-hunt", "/location-quest", "/tech-tree"];
pub const REPOINTED_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 2;

; HTTP routes, merged into the public router at src/api/mod.rs:89, :91 and :97.
pub const CATALOG_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 27;
pub const QUEST_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 13;
pub const TECH_TREE_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 4;
pub const LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 44;

; The footprint this file can name file by file. 181 is every .rs under src/.
pub const TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT : u16 = 181;
pub const LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT : u16 = 25;
pub const LEGACY_SOURCE_LOC : u16 = 9193;
pub const SURVEY_LOC_CLAIM_REPRODUCED : bool = false;
pub const SURVEY_LOC_CLAIM_NOTE : str = "The survey reported about 9523 LOC across 26 of the 181 src/*.rs files. 181 reproduces exactly. 9523 and 26 do not: no tracked file in the repository carries the number 9523 -- git grep -l 9523 returns nothing, and the matches an unfiltered recursive grep finds are incidental digit runs inside target/ build fingerprints, not sources -- and no nameable list of legacy-domain modules sums to it. The 25 files and 9193 lines pinned here are a list that can be printed and re-added, which is the only kind of footprint number this corpus accepts. The difference is not asserted to be an arithmetic error in the survey -- it is an unreproducible figure, and an unreproducible figure is reported as such rather than inherited.";

pub fn legacy_footprint_is_measured(files_named: u16, total_files: u16, loc: u16) bool {
    if (files_named == 0 or loc == 0) {
        return false;
    }
    return files_named < total_files;
}

; --- Claiming a surface is gone ------------------------------------------------------------------
; turbobaby/publication's principle, applied to retirement: nothing here claims a surface is gone
; without evidence. The garden route is the one surface that passes -- a search for a garden route
; declaration over src/ returns zero. The trap is the same search run on the bare WORD: the client
; router still carries the word on four LINES (src/ui/routes.rs:57, :58, :61 and :97 -- five
; occurrences, four lines, and the constant below counts lines) because the record of
; the removal lives in comments, exactly as the allowlist witness explains at :176-182. A word
; count is not absence evidence; a declaration count is.
pub const GARDEN_ROUTE_DECLARATIONS : u16 = 0;
pub const GARDEN_WORD_HITS_IN_CLIENT_ROUTER : u16 = 4;
pub const COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT : u8 = 1;

pub fn may_claim_surface_is_gone(route_declarations: u16, handler_definitions: u16, screen_definitions: u16) bool {
    return route_declarations == 0 and handler_definitions == 0 and screen_definitions == 0;
}

; An orphaned asset is none of the three states: no data was hidden, no table was dropped and no
; route reaches it. It is shipped bytes with one textual reference, and that reference is a
; comment. The asset is assets/game/catch.js, 13270 bytes, and the one textual reference to it
; in shipped source is the comment at assets/game/ride.js:1066 -- a search for the filename over
; the working tree, excluding .git and target/, returns that line and the sibling contract named
; below and nothing else. The count is this file's; whether any code mounts the asset is
; turbobaby/game-score's measurement, consumed here as a boolean rather than re-measured.
pub const ORPHAN_ASSET_TEXT_REFERENCES : u16 = 1;

pub fn asset_is_orphaned(mounted_by_code: bool, code_references: u16, comment_references: u16) bool {
    if (mounted_by_code) {
        return false;
    }
    return code_references == 0 and comment_references > 0;
}

; --- The refusal ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; This contract classifies. It does not choose. Which of the eight live legacy paths goes next,
; and in what order, is the owner's call and issue #2's scope; epic #26 keeps that issue open and
; ties it to no date. A ranking invented here would read as a plan and would be obeyed.
pub const THIS_FILE_PICKS_THE_NEXT_SURFACE : bool = false;
pub const THIS_FILE_CARRIES_A_DELETION_DATE : bool = false;
pub const RETIREMENT_ORDER_IS_PUBLISHED : bool = false;
pub const NEXT_SURFACE_NOTE : str = "No source in this repository ranks the legacy surfaces. Issue #2 is OPEN and states a rename task with an acceptance grep, not an order of removal; epic #26 workstream 3 lists the surfaces to remove and fixes no sequence and no date; DECISIONS.md D19 says in terms that the fate of the legacy screens is a product call and that the data waits, hidden, until the owner makes it. What is missing is the owner's ranking, and no measurement could substitute for it: every one of the eight routes is equally reachable, so reachability cannot break the tie, and a guess dressed as a contract would be followed. This file therefore classifies each surface and stops.";

pub fn next_surface_is_decided_here(owner_has_ranked: bool) bool {
    return false;
}

; --- Tests -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test the_three_partial_states_are_named_and_the_value_set_is_closed {
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES.len == PARTIAL_STATE_COUNT;
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_COUNT == 3;
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES[0] == "data_hidden";
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES[1] == "surface_live";
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES[2] == "reader_allowlisted";
    assert state_is_known(STATE_LIVE) == true;
    assert state_is_known(STATE_FULLY_RETIRED) == true;
    assert state_is_known(STATE_COUNT) == false;
}

test each_of_the_three_partial_states_is_reachable_and_distinct {
    assert retirement_state(false, false, false, true) == STATE_DATA_HIDDEN;
    assert retirement_state(true, false, false, false) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE;
    assert retirement_state(false, true, true, false) == STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED;
    assert retirement_state(false, true, false, false) == STATE_FULLY_RETIRED;
    assert retirement_state(false, false, false, false) == STATE_LIVE;
}

test a_hidden_row_is_not_a_retired_surface {
    assert retirement_state(true, false, false, true) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE;
    assert surface_is_retired(true, false, false, true) == false;
    assert surface_is_retired(false, false, false, true) == false;
    assert data_decision_changes_the_surface(true, false) == false;
    assert data_decision_changes_the_surface(false, true) == false;
    assert data_decision_changes_the_surface(true, true) == false;
}

test a_reachable_surface_outranks_every_decision_beneath_it {
    assert retirement_state(true, true, true, true) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE;
    assert retirement_state(true, true, false, false) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE;
    assert surface_is_retired(true, true, false, false) == false;
}

test only_the_completed_state_counts_as_a_retired_surface {
    assert surface_is_retired(false, true, false, false) == true;
    assert surface_is_retired(false, true, true, false) == false;
    assert surface_is_retired(false, false, false, false) == false;
}

test migration_085_has_the_shape_d19_mandates {
    assert HIDDEN_TABLES.len == HIDDEN_TABLE_COUNT;
    assert HIDDEN_TABLE_COUNT == 6;
    assert HIDDEN_TABLES[0] == "events";
    assert HIDDEN_TABLES[5] == "sets";
    assert HIDING_ROW_DELETES == 0;
    assert HIDING_TABLE_DROPS == 0;
    assert HIDING_VISIBILITY_UPDATES == 6;
    assert hiding_migration_is_conformant(HIDING_ROW_DELETES, HIDING_TABLE_DROPS, HIDING_VISIBILITY_UPDATES) == true;
}

test a_migration_that_deletes_or_drops_is_not_a_hiding_migration {
    assert hiding_migration_is_conformant(1, 0, 6) == false;
    assert hiding_migration_is_conformant(0, 1, 6) == false;
    assert hiding_migration_is_conformant(0, 0, 0) == false;
    assert hidden_data_is_reversible(true, true) == true;
    assert hidden_data_is_reversible(false, true) == false;
    assert hidden_data_is_reversible(true, false) == false;
}

test migration_083_drops_six_tables_and_one_of_them_keeps_every_reader {
    assert DROPPED_TABLES.len == DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT;
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT == 6;
    assert DROPPED_TABLES[0] == "lab_certificates";
    assert DROPPED_TABLES[2] == "strains";
    assert DROPPED_TABLES[5] == "garden_config";
    assert DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_A_SURVIVING_READER == 1;
    assert DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_NO_READER == 5;
    assert DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_A_SURVIVING_READER + DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_NO_READER == DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT;
}

test this_file_owns_both_numbers_that_bot_surface_copies {
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE == true;
    assert ALLOWLIST_SIZE_IS_OWNED_HERE == true;
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPIED_BY_ID == "turbobaby/bot-surface";
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPIED_BY_ID == REUSES_BOT_SURFACE_ID;
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPIED_BY_ID != ID;
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPY_DECLARATION == "LEGACY_TABLES_DROPPED_BY_THAT_MIGRATION";
    assert ALLOWLIST_SIZE_COPY_DECLARATION == "LEGACY_SURVIVOR_ENTRY_COUNT";
    assert DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT_COPY_DECLARATION != ALLOWLIST_SIZE_COPY_DECLARATION;
}

test the_retirement_distinction_is_still_declared_nowhere_else {
    assert CORPUS_FILE_COUNT == 43;
    assert CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE == 42;
    assert SPECS_CONTAINING_THE_WORD_RETIRE_2026_09_21 == 16;
    assert SPECS_DECLARING_THE_RETIREMENT_DISTINCTION_2026_09_21 == 0;
    assert SPECS_CONTAINING_THE_WORD_RETIRE_2026_09_21 > SPECS_DECLARING_THE_RETIREMENT_DISTINCTION_2026_09_21;
    assert SPECS_CONTAINING_THE_WORD_RETIRE_2026_09_21 < CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE;
    assert THE_WORD_IS_SHARED_THE_SUBJECT_IS_NOT == true;
}

test the_allowlist_is_pinned_by_size_and_rule_not_by_contents {
    assert ALLOWLIST_SIZE == 4;
    assert ALLOWLIST_DISTINCT_TABLES == 1;
    assert ALLOWLIST_DISTINCT_TABLES < DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT;
    assert ALLOWLIST_CHECK_COUNT == 3;
    assert ALLOWLIST_DETECTION_SHAPE_COUNT == 3;
    assert ALLOWLIST_TABLE_POSITION_KEYWORDS == 5;
}

test an_allowlist_entry_needs_a_path_a_table_a_reason_and_a_live_match {
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, true, 41, true) == true;
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(false, true, 41, true) == false;
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, false, 41, true) == false;
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, true, 41, false) == false;
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, true, 40, true) == false;
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, true, 0, true) == false;
}

test the_allowlist_is_checked_from_both_ends {
    assert allowlist_is_sound(true, true, true) == true;
    assert allowlist_is_sound(false, true, true) == false;
    assert allowlist_is_sound(true, false, true) == false;
    assert allowlist_is_sound(true, true, false) == false;
}

test keeping_something_requires_naming_it_with_a_reason {
    assert keeping_is_permitted(true, 41) == true;
    assert keeping_is_permitted(false, 41) == false;
    assert keeping_is_permitted(true, 40) == false;
    assert keeping_is_permitted(false, 0) == false;
}

test the_retired_set_is_derived_rather_than_listed {
    assert retired_set_is_trustworthy(true, true, true) == true;
    assert retired_set_is_trustworthy(false, true, true) == false;
    assert retired_set_is_trustworthy(true, false, true) == false;
    assert retired_set_is_trustworthy(true, true, false) == false;
}

test the_live_legacy_surface_is_counted_and_repointed_paths_are_counted_apart {
    assert LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES.len == LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTE_COUNT;
    assert LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTE_COUNT == 8;
    assert LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES[0] == "/accessories";
    assert LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES[3] == "/game";
    assert LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES[7] == "/tech-tree";
    assert REPOINTED_ROUTE_COUNT == 2;
}

test the_legacy_http_route_total_is_the_sum_of_its_three_modules {
    assert CATALOG_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == 27;
    assert QUEST_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == 13;
    assert TECH_TREE_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == 4;
    assert CATALOG_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT + QUEST_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT + TECH_TREE_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT;
    assert LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == 44;
}

test the_footprint_is_a_list_that_can_be_re_added {
    assert TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT == 181;
    assert LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT == 25;
    assert LEGACY_SOURCE_LOC == 9193;
    assert legacy_footprint_is_measured(LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT, TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT, LEGACY_SOURCE_LOC) == true;
    assert legacy_footprint_is_measured(0, TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT, LEGACY_SOURCE_LOC) == false;
    assert legacy_footprint_is_measured(LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT, TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT, 0) == false;
    assert SURVEY_LOC_CLAIM_REPRODUCED == false;
}

test a_gone_surface_is_proved_by_declarations_not_by_a_word_count {
    assert may_claim_surface_is_gone(GARDEN_ROUTE_DECLARATIONS, 0, 0) == true;
    assert GARDEN_ROUTE_DECLARATIONS == 0;
    assert GARDEN_WORD_HITS_IN_CLIENT_ROUTER == 4;
    assert GARDEN_WORD_HITS_IN_CLIENT_ROUTER > GARDEN_ROUTE_DECLARATIONS;
    assert COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT == 1;
}

test a_surviving_declaration_of_any_kind_defeats_the_claim {
    assert may_claim_surface_is_gone(1, 0, 0) == false;
    assert may_claim_surface_is_gone(0, 1, 0) == false;
    assert may_claim_surface_is_gone(0, 0, 1) == false;
}

test an_orphaned_asset_is_none_of_the_three_states {
    assert asset_is_orphaned(false, 0, ORPHAN_ASSET_TEXT_REFERENCES) == true;
    assert asset_is_orphaned(true, 0, 1) == false;
    assert asset_is_orphaned(false, 1, 1) == false;
    assert asset_is_orphaned(false, 0, 0) == false;
    assert ORPHAN_ASSET_TEXT_REFERENCES == 1;
}

test the_reuse_edges_are_named_and_no_sibling_decision_is_restated {
    assert REUSES_BOT_SURFACE_ID == "turbobaby/bot-surface";
    assert REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID == "turbobaby/catalog-api";
    assert REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID == "turbobaby/availability";
    assert REUSES_PUBLICATION_ID == "turbobaby/publication";
    assert REUSES_DELIVERY_TERMS_ID == "turbobaby/delivery-terms";
    assert REUSES_GAME_SCORE_ID == "turbobaby/game-score";
    assert REUSES_RIDE_GAME_ID == "turbobaby/ride-game";
    assert REUSE_EDGE_COUNT == 7;
}

test this_file_refuses_to_choose_the_next_surface {
    assert THIS_FILE_PICKS_THE_NEXT_SURFACE == false;
    assert THIS_FILE_CARRIES_A_DELETION_DATE == false;
    assert RETIREMENT_ORDER_IS_PUBLISHED == false;
    assert next_surface_is_decided_here(true) == false;
    assert next_surface_is_decided_here(false) == false;
}

test the_identity_of_this_contract_is_fixed {
    assert ID == "turbobaby/legacy-retirement";
    assert KIND == "retirement-contract";
    assert ISSUE == "#2";
    assert EPIC == "#26";
    assert DECISIONS == "DECISIONS.md D5, D19";
}

; --- Invariants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

invariant a_hidden_row_never_retires_a_reachable_surface
    assert retirement_state(true, false, false, true) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE and surface_is_retired(true, false, false, true) == false

invariant hiding_data_alone_never_retires_anything
    assert surface_is_retired(false, false, false, true) == false and data_decision_changes_the_surface(true, true) == false

invariant a_reachable_legacy_surface_always_reports_the_same_state
    assert retirement_state(true, true, true, true) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE and retirement_state(true, false, false, false) == STATE_SURFACE_LIVE

invariant an_allowlisted_reader_is_not_a_retired_surface
    assert retirement_state(false, true, true, false) == STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED and surface_is_retired(false, true, true, false) == false

invariant the_three_partial_states_stay_three_and_stay_named
    assert PARTIAL_STATE_NAMES.len == PARTIAL_STATE_COUNT and PARTIAL_STATE_COUNT == 3 and STATE_COUNT == 5

invariant a_hiding_migration_that_deletes_a_row_stops_being_one
    assert hiding_migration_is_conformant(1, 0, 6) == false and hiding_migration_is_conformant(0, 1, 6) == false

invariant every_dropped_table_is_accounted_for_on_exactly_one_side
    assert DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_A_SURVIVING_READER + DROPPED_TABLES_WITH_NO_READER == DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT and DROPPED_TABLES.len == DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT

invariant a_kept_reader_without_a_named_reason_is_never_permitted
    assert keeping_is_permitted(true, ALLOWLIST_REASON_MIN_CHARS) == false and keeping_is_permitted(false, 4000) == false

invariant an_allowlist_entry_that_matches_nothing_is_invalid
    assert allowlist_entry_is_valid(true, true, 4000, false) == false and allowlist_is_sound(true, false, true) == false

invariant the_legacy_http_total_cannot_drift_from_its_parts
    assert CATALOG_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT + QUEST_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT + TECH_TREE_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT == LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT

invariant no_surface_is_claimed_gone_while_any_declaration_survives
    assert may_claim_surface_is_gone(1, 0, 0) == false and may_claim_surface_is_gone(0, 1, 0) == false and may_claim_surface_is_gone(0, 0, 1) == false

invariant a_word_count_is_never_absence_evidence
    assert GARDEN_WORD_HITS_IN_CLIENT_ROUTER > 0 and may_claim_surface_is_gone(GARDEN_ROUTE_DECLARATIONS, 0, 0) == true

invariant an_unreproducible_footprint_figure_is_never_adopted
    assert SURVEY_LOC_CLAIM_REPRODUCED == false and LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT < TOTAL_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT

invariant this_file_never_chooses_the_next_surface_or_a_date
    assert next_surface_is_decided_here(true) == false and THIS_FILE_PICKS_THE_NEXT_SURFACE == false and THIS_FILE_CARRIES_A_DELETION_DATE == false and RETIREMENT_ORDER_IS_PUBLISHED == false
